          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Tales by Dots and Lines"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.847,
            0.128
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The mean of the new collection also increases by 10. Notice that the relative position of the mean stays the same."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.219,
            0.13,
            0.79,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "chart_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.219,
                0.13,
                0.79,
                0.221
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_chart_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.244,
            0.727,
            0.265
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We get the following dot plot if we reduce every value by 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.267,
            0.789,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "chart_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.222,
                0.267,
                0.789,
                0.357
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_chart_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.37,
            0.53,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This can be explained using algebra —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.389,
            0.845,
            0.429
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose there are n values in the collection. Let these values be represented by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "X _ { 1 } , X _ { 2 } , X _ { 3 } , \\ldots X _ { n } ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Their average is given by —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.392,
            0.432,
            0.608,
            0.462
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{X_{1}+X_{2}+X_{3}+\\cdots+X_{n}}{n}=a."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.464,
            0.845,
            0.502
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When a fixed number, for example, 3 is added to every value in the collection, the new average becomes —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.503,
            0.664,
            0.627
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{\\overbrace{x_{1}+3)_{+}(x_{2}+3)_{+}(x_{3}+3)_{+}\\cdots+(x_{n}+3)}^{n}}{n}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.632,
            0.772,
            0.653
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "That is, the new average is 3 more than the previous average."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.654,
            0.808,
            0.695
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Try to explain, using algebra, what the average is when a fixed number, e.g., 2 is subtracted from every value in the collection."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.7,
            0.808,
            0.742
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Try to explain this using the fair-share interpretation of average that you learnt last year."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.82,
            0.652,
            0.924,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 13,
              "bbox": [
                0.82,
                0.652,
                0.924,
                0.763
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_image_13.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.755,
            0.808,
            0.794
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ What happens to the average if every value in the collection is doubled?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.798,
            0.847,
            0.838
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You may have guessed that the average also doubles. The following is an example with the data we saw earlier —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
